.TH "C3F" "1" "2026-11-11"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
\fBc3f\fR - a stable, fast, token-based formatter for C3
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBc3f\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR .\&.\&.\&]
.br
\fBc3f\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB-\fR
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBc3f\fR formats C3 source files and checks every result by lexing it again and comparing it,
token by token, with the input.\& A place it cannot verify, or that is unbalanced (a bracket
still being typed), is kept as written, so it is safe to run on a file while editing it.\&
.PP
A bracket that is never closed, and a raw string (backtick) or doc comment that is never
terminated, damage the file from there on.\& c3f picks it up again at the next line that
starts at column 0 with a top-level declaration (\fBfn\fR, \fBmacro\fR, \fBstruct\fR, \fBunion\fR, \fBenum\fR,
\fBbitstruct\fR, \fBinterface\fR, \fBfaultdef\fR, \fBalias\fR, \fBtypedef\fR, \fBconst\fR, \fBconstdef\fR, \fBconstset\fR, \fBmodule\fR,
\fBimport\fR, \fBextern\fR, \fBattrdef\fR, \fBattrmacro\fR) or with a doc comment (\fB<*\fR).\& The text from the error
to there is kept byte for byte as written, and nothing is inserted or changed; from there on the
file is formatted as usual.\& \fB$if\fR and the other \fB$\fR keywords do not count, as code may write
them flush left inside a function.\& Without such a line the rest of the file is kept.\& Each one is a
note on standard error with its line: \fBunclosed '\&{'\&\fR, \fBunterminated raw string\fR or \fBunterminated
doc comment\fR, followed by \fBkept as written up to line N\fR (\fBto the end of the file\fR if nothing is
picked up again).\& A block comment that runs to the end of the file is valid code (the rest of the
file is a comment): it is kept as written, without a note.\&
.PP
With one file and none of \fB-w\fR, \fB--check\fR and \fB--diff\fR, the formatted file is written to
standard output.\& With \fB-\fR, standard input is read and the result written to standard output.\&
For directories, every file ending in \fI.\&c3\fR, \fI.\&c3i\fR and \fI.\&c3t\fR below them is formatted;
hidden directories and those named \fIbuild\fR or \fIlib\fR are skipped, and links are not followed
(a file named on the command line is).\& Files are replaced atomically.\&
.PP
The code between the comments \fB// c3f off\fR and \fB// c3f on\fR is left untouched.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-w\fR, \fB--write\fR
.RS 4
Rewrite the files in place.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--check\fR
.RS 4
Write nothing; list the files that would change.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--diff\fR
.RS 4
Print a unified diff of the changes.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--config\fR \fIfile\fR
.RS 4
Use this \fI.\&editorconfig\fR instead of searching upward from each file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--set\fR \fIkey\fR=\fIvalue\fR
.RS 4
Set an option (see \fBCONFIGURATION\fR); repeatable, applied after \fI.\&editorconfig\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--print-config\fR
.RS 4
Print the options in effect for the file and where each comes from.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--stdin-filename\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
With \fB-\fR, the path used to find \fI.\&editorconfig\fR and in messages.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--stdin\fR, \fB--stdout\fR, \fB--stdin-filepath\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
The same as \fB-\fR, the default output (to standard output; it cannot be combined with \fB-w\fR,
\fB--check\fR, \fB--diff\fR and \fB--print-config\fR) and \fB--stdin-filename\fR.\& They are the flags the
C3 extension for VS Code passes to the formatter set in its \fIc3.\&format.\&path\fR setting.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--exclude\fR \fIglob\fR
.RS 4
Skip matching paths; repeatable.\& A glob is matched against the path below the directory
given, and against each part of it that starts after a \fI/\fR: \fIgen/*\fR skips
\fIsrc/gen/a.\&c3\fR as well.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--git-hook\fR
.RS 4
Install a pre-commit hook in this git repository that rejects commits with unformatted
C3 files.\& An existing hook is kept.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
.RS 4
Print the usage.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--version\fR
.RS 4
Print the version.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Options are read from \fI.\&editorconfig\fR files: the nearest file wins, and \fIroot = true\fR stops
the search.\& The standard keys (\fBindent_style\fR, \fBindent_size\fR, \fBtab_width\fR, \fBend_of_line\fR,
\fBinsert_final_newline\fR, \fBmax_line_length\fR) are used as they are, and the keys beginning with
\fIc3f_\fR are c3f'\&s own.\& For example:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
[*\&.{c3,c3i,c3t}]
indent_style = tab
max_line_length = 100
c3f_line_breaks = wrap
.fi
.RE
.PP
Values are given with their default first.\&
.PP
\fBc3f_style\fR = stdlib | knr | strict
.RS 4
A preset, applied before the other options, which override it.\& \fBstdlib\fR is the style of
the C3 standard library.\& \fBknr\fR uses K&R braces, also for functions, and \fB} else {\fR.\&
\fBstrict\fR is \fBstdlib\fR with the spacing made uniform where the standard library itself
varies: \fIFoo* p\fR, padded initializer braces, tight slices, and sorted imports.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBindent_style\fR = tab | space
.RS 4
Indent with tabs or spaces.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBindent_size\fR = 4
.RS 4
1 to 16, or \fItab\fR (the value of \fBtab_width\fR).\& The width of one level with spaces.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBtab_width\fR = 4
.RS 4
1 to 16.\& The width of a tab, for aligning and for the line length.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBend_of_line\fR = keep | lf | crlf
.RS 4
The line ending.\& \fBkeep\fR uses the file'\&s own.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBinsert_final_newline\fR = true | false
.RS 4
End the file with a line break.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBmax_line_length\fR = off
.RS 4
\fBoff\fR, or 1 to 10000.\& The column limit used by wrapping and alignment.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_line_breaks\fR = keep | wrap | wrap_rewrite | reflow
.RS 4
What \fBc3f\fR may do with line breaks.\& It needs a \fBmax_line_length\fR.\& \fBkeep\fR never
moves them; \fBwrap\fR breaks the statements that have a line over the limit; \fBreflow\fR
also lays out again every statement that spans several lines, so a break made by hand
is joined if the statement fits on one line.\& A statement on one line that fits is
never touched.\& \fBwrap_rewrite\fR is \fBwrap\fR, and in addition:
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
a string literal that still runs past the limit is written as several literals,
.PD
.RE
which the compiler joins: "a b c" becomes "a " "b c".\& It cuts after a space if it can,
.RS 4
never inside an escape sequence, a UTF-8 character or a \fBprintf\fR conversion, and not in
an attribute, an \fBassert\fR or a compile-time directive.\& The value of every piece is
checked to be the original'\&s.\&
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
the single statement after an \fBif\fR, \fBelse\fR, \fBwhile\fR, \fBfor\fR or \fBforeach\fR without braces
.PD
.RE
that is too long for its line gets braces and a line of its own (\fBc3c\fR does not accept the
.RS 4
statement of an \fBif\fR on the line after it, so it could only be broken inside).\& Bodies that
start with another \fBif\fR, a loop, a \fBswitch\fR or a \fBdefer\fR are left as they are.\&
Only this option changes more than whitespace.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_brace_style\fR = allman | knr | linux
.RS 4
Where the opening brace goes.\& \fBlinux\fR is \fBknr\fR with the braces of functions on their
own line.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_else_style\fR = follow | own_line | same_line
.RS 4
Where \fBelse\fR goes: \fBfollow\fR the brace style, on its own line, or after \fB}\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_while_style\fR = keep | own_line | same_line
.RS 4
Where the \fBwhile\fR of a \fBdo\fR loop goes: as written, on its own line, or after the \fB}\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_one_line_blocks\fR = keep | expand
.RS 4
Keep a block written on one line, or put its statements on lines of their own.\& \fBexpand\fR also
breaks the line after every \fB;\fR that ends a statement (not in the header of a \fBfor\fR or \fB$for\fR,
and not before a comment), and after the \fB}\fR of a block.\& In a compile-time block the header,
\fB$else\fR and \fB$endif\fR (and the other end keywords) stand alone on their lines; the body of a
\fB$case\fR or \fBcase\fR on the line of its label stays, as does a single \fBif (x) return;\fR.\& A
multi-line initializer starts its elements on the line after its \fB{\fR, and its \fB}\fR goes on a
line of its own after a trailing comma; an initializer on one line is not touched.\&
The body of a \fBstruct\fR, \fBunion\fR, \fBenum\fR, \fBconstdef\fR, \fBbitstruct\fR or \fBinterface\fR written on
one line is written on several, one member or enum value per line, and so is a \fBfaultdef\fR
with more than one member.\& The braces of an empty body are placed as the brace style says
(Allman: \fBfn void f()\fR and \fB{}\fR on the next line; K&R: \fB{}\fR on the line); the \fB{}\fR stays
together, and a lambda keeps its braces where they are.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_case_indent\fR = indent | flush
.RS 4
Indent \fBcase\fR under \fBswitch\fR, or put it in the same column.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_compile_time_indent\fR = keep | indent | flush
.RS 4
The contents of \fB$if\fR, \fB$switch\fR and \fB$foreach\fR blocks: as written, indented, or at the
level of the directive.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_continuation\fR = keep | indent | align
.RS 4
How the lines of a broken statement are continued: as written, one more level, or
aligned under the opening bracket.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_spacing\fR = stdlib | strict
.RS 4
Where the standard library writes both forms (about 0.\&2% of its spacing), \fBstdlib\fR
keeps what was written and \fBstrict\fR always writes the more common one.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_space_after_cast\fR = false | true
.RS 4
A space after a cast: \fI(int)x\fR or \fI(int) x\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_pointer_style\fR = keep | type | name
.RS 4
Write \fIFoo* p\fR (\fBtype\fR) or \fIFoo *p\fR (\fBname\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_space_inside_brackets\fR = keep | false | true
.RS 4
Spaces inside \fI[ ]\fR: \fIa[i]\fR (\fBfalse\fR) or \fIa[ i ]\fR (\fBtrue\fR).\& Parentheses are not touched.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_space_inside_braces\fR = keep | false | true
.RS 4
Spaces inside the braces of an initializer list: \fI{1, 2}\fR (\fBfalse\fR) or \fI{ 1, 2 }\fR
(\fBtrue\fR).\& The braces of blocks and bodies are not touched.\& With \fBkeep\fR, \fBc3f_spacing\fR =
\fBstrict\fR pads them (\fI{ 1, 2 }\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_max_blank_lines\fR = 2
.RS 4
0 to 100.\& More blank lines in a row are cut to this number.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_trim_block_blanks\fR = true | false
.RS 4
Remove blank lines after an opening and before a closing brace.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_blank_lines_between_decls\fR = keep | 1
.RS 4
\fB1\fR puts exactly one blank line between declarations.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_align\fR = keep | decls | off
.RS 4
Align the names, \fI=\fR and \fI=>\fR of consecutive lines (\fBdecls\fR), keep the alignment as
written (\fBkeep\fR), or remove it (\fBoff\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_align_comments\fR = keep | always | off
.RS 4
The same for trailing comments.\& The spaces and tabs at the end of a \fI//\fR comment are
always removed.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_trailing_comment_spaces\fR = keep
.RS 4
\fBkeep\fR, or 1 to 16.\& The spaces before a trailing \fI//\fR comment.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_magic_comma\fR = true | false
.RS 4
A trailing comma keeps one item per line when wrapping.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_soft_max_line_length\fR = 0
.RS 4
0 to 10000.\& A second, soft limit for wrapping: every column past it costs
\fBc3f_wrap_cost_soft\fR, so a line is broken earlier than \fBmax_line_length\fR if that is cheaper.\&
0 is not a switch: it puts the limit at column 0, so every column costs the same and
the line breaks stay where \fBmax_line_length\fR puts them.\& With \fBc3f_line_breaks\fR = \fBreflow\fR,
a statement written on one line is left alone when this is 0 and laid out again otherwise.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_wrap_cost_hard\fR = 100
.RS 4
The cost of a column past \fBmax_line_length\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_wrap_cost_soft\fR = 0.\&05
.RS 4
The cost of a column past \fBc3f_soft_max_line_length\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_wrap_cost_break\fR = 2
.RS 4
The cost of a line break.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_wrap_max_tokens\fR = 2000
.RS 4
0 to 10000.\& Statements of more tokens are not wrapped.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBc3f_sort_imports\fR = off | lines | lists | all | split
.RS 4
Reorder imports.\& \fBlines\fR sorts the statements of a run (no blank line between them),
\fBlists\fR the modules inside one statement, \fBall\fR both, and \fBsplit\fR also writes one module
per statement (a statement with a comment is only sorted).\& The \fBstrict\fR style uses
\fBall\fR; an explicit value wins.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
Success.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB1\fR
.RS 4
\fB--check\fR found files that would change.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB2\fR
.RS 4
Usage or I/O error.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB3\fR
.RS 4
\fB--check\fR found a place it kept as written.\& With \fB-w\fR, \fB--diff\fR or when printing the
result, that is a success (exit status 0), with the notes on standard error.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Format a project in place:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
c3f -w src/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Fail a CI job if anything is not formatted:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
c3f --check \&.
.fi
.RE
.PP
Format in an editor, with the path used for \fI.\&editorconfig\fR:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
c3f --stdin-filename src/main\&.c3 -
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
\fI.\&editorconfig\fR
.RS 4
The options, found by searching upward from each file.\&
.PP
.RE
